================================================================================
UPSTREAM FRAMEWORK
================================================================================

nnU-Net v2
    Copyright © Division of Medical Image Computing, German Cancer Research
    Center (DKFZ).
    Paper: Isensee, F., Jaeger, P.F., Kohl, S.A.A., Petersen, J., &
    Maier-Hein, K.H. (2021). "nnU-Net: a self-configuring method for deep
    learning-based biomedical image segmentation." Nature Methods,
    18(2), 203-211.
    Source: https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet
    License: Apache License 2.0

    Camylanet is a wrapper / derivative framework that extends nnU-Net v2
    with a curated set of architecture variants and a simplified API.

================================================================================
BUNDLED ARCHITECTURE IMPLEMENTATIONS
================================================================================

The following network architectures are shipped under
`camylanet/network_architecture/` (and subdirectories). Each entry lists the
original publication and any upstream reference implementation we adapted.

1. nnU-Net (Convolutional, 2D + 3D)
   Isensee et al., Nature Methods, 2021.
   https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet

2. SwinUNETR (Transformer, 2D + 3D)
   Hatamizadeh et al., "Swin UNETR: Swin Transformers for Semantic
   Segmentation of Brain Tumors in MRI Images", 2022.
   Reference implementation from MONAI
   (https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI), license: Apache-2.0.

3. SegResNet (Convolutional, 2D + 3D)
   Myronenko, "3D MRI brain tumor segmentation using autoencoder
   regularization", MICCAI BrainLes, 2018.
   Reference implementation from MONAI
   (https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI), license: Apache-2.0.

4. U-Net++ (Convolutional, 2D + 3D)
   Zhou et al., "UNet++: A Nested U-Net Architecture for Medical Image
   Segmentation", DLMIA/MLMI, 2018.
   Reference implementation from MONAI
   (https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI), license: Apache-2.0.

5. U-Mamba (State-space, 2D + 3D)
   Ma, Li, Wang, "U-Mamba: Enhancing Long-range Dependency for Biomedical
   Image Segmentation", 2024.
   https://github.com/bowang-lab/U-Mamba
   License: Apache-2.0.

6. MedNeXt (Convolutional, 3D)
   Roy et al., "MedNeXt: Transformer-driven Scaling of ConvNets for
   Medical Image Segmentation", MICCAI, 2023.
   https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/MedNeXt
   License: Apache-2.0.

7. 3D UX-Net (Transformer, 3D)
   Lee et al., "3D UX-Net: A Large Kernel Volumetric ConvNet Modernizing
   Hierarchical Transformer for Medical Image Segmentation", ICLR, 2023.
   https://github.com/MASILab/3DUX-Net
   License: Apache-2.0.

8. UNETR (Transformer, 3D)
   Hatamizadeh et al., "UNETR: Transformers for 3D Medical Image
   Segmentation", WACV, 2022.
   Reference implementation from MONAI
   (https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI), license: Apache-2.0.

9. nnFormer (Transformer, 3D)
   Zhou et al., "nnFormer: Volumetric Medical Image Segmentation via a
   3D Transformer", 2022.
   https://github.com/282857341/nnFormer
   License: MIT.

10. STU-Net (Convolutional, 3D)
    Huang et al., "STU-Net: Scalable and Transferable Medical Image
    Segmentation Models Empowered by Large-Scale Supervised Pre-training",
    2023.
    https://github.com/uni-medical/STU-Net
    License: Apache-2.0.

11. TransUNet (Transformer, 2D)
    Chen et al., "TransUNet: Transformers Make Strong Encoders for
    Medical Image Segmentation", 2021.
    https://github.com/Beckschen/TransUNet
    License: Apache-2.0.

12. UTNet (Transformer, 2D)
    Gao et al., "UTNet: A Hybrid Transformer Architecture for Medical
    Image Segmentation", MICCAI, 2021.
    https://github.com/yhygao/UTNet
    License: BSD 3-Clause.

13. SwinUMamba (State-space, 2D)
    Liu et al., "Swin-UMamba: Mamba-based UNet with ImageNet-based
    pretraining", 2024.
    https://github.com/JiarunLiu/Swin-UMamba
    License: Apache-2.0.

14. U-KAN (Convolutional, 2D)
    Li et al., "U-KAN Makes Strong Backbone for Medical Image Segmentation
    and Generation", 2024.
    https://github.com/CUHK-AIM-Group/U-KAN
    License: (see upstream repository).

================================================================================
OTHER SHIPPED BUILDING BLOCKS
================================================================================

`camylanet/network_architecture/custom/` and `custom_modules/` contain
auxiliary convolutional / attention blocks used by one or more of the
architectures above. These are either original to camylanet or adapted
from MONAI (https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI, Apache-2.0) and the
upstream reference implementations listed above.

